          {
            "text": "Possible harmful algal bloom - avoid contact with the water: Keep out of the water and keep children and dogs out, including from spray. Do not let animals drink it. Report the bloom to your local environmental agency - only a laboratory can confirm whether it is toxin-producing cyanobacteria. Confirm the observation in the app to raise this to a full alert."
          },
          {
            "text": "Conditions suit mosquito breeding: Remove containers and litter that hold water near the bank, and tell the municipality about standing water that does not drain. Restoring flow is the durable fix; insecticide is not, and it removes the stream's own insect life along with the mosquitoes."
          }
